## GO-5 — discharged, and it caught a shipped defect that three cross-vendor reviews approved

Performed 2026-09-17/18 against the merged tree. **The obligation earned its existence here.**

**How the range was built**, as GO-5 requires, because R-2's measurement — re-derived at the gate as
**42 of 42** integration branches contained in `main` — means no ticket in this backlog has a
non-empty one. A scratch ticket `Q-0136` was created, `harness/Q-0136/integration` cut from `main`,
and three markdown notes committed on `harness/Q-0136/implement` alone, giving an
`integration...implement` range of **897 bytes** across 3 files. `repo.max_diff_bytes` was lowered
to **400** so the case is **truncated** with one file omitted entirely. Everything else — the
daemon, the engine, the flow, the gate, the route, the browser — is the shipped product; only the
vendor CLI is mocked, through `--adapter mock`.

### What it rendered BEFORE the fix, which is why this obligation exists

A chore run parked at its review exhaustion gate, `reached.stepId = review`. `runs.log` for that run
records, twice, on consecutive lines:

    run=9 diff truncated range=harness/Q-0136/integration...harness/Q-0136/implement limit=400
          kept=400 of 897 — no patch at all for 1 file(s): demo/only9.md
    run=9 step=review vendor=mock model=- verdict=revise

and the gate screen said, of that same step:

    The step whose decision reached this gate was given no diff, so there is nothing to show here.

**That sentence was false.** `GET /runs/run-1/gates/9:4/diff` answered `no-diff`. The cause is
`steps.ts`'s `promptContext`, an explicit literal narrowing the run context field by field, which
did not forward `reportDiff` — optional on `DiffContext`, so its absence typechecks, lints and
passes every suite. The **run-level preflight** path kept working; the **step-time** path captured
nothing, which is **186 of 208 materialisations** in this repository's history and **every chore
run** — verbatim the blindness `diff.ts`'s own capture comment describes and AC-1 exists to forbid,
reproduced one layer up in a different file. Fixed by hand after the gate on Q-0073's and Q-0080's
precedent, pinned by `prompt-context.source.test.ts`, and shown red by mutation.

### What it renders AFTER the fix, transcribed from the browser

    The decision that reached this gate   revise
    Step: review
    mock code-reviewer:verdict #1
    MAJOR   major: src/mock.ts:1 (mock) placeholder finding

    The diff that decision was made on    Given to step: review
    Range: harness/Q-0136/integration...harness/Q-0136/implement
    This diff was cut before that step saw all of it, so the review below it covers less than the change.
    400 of 897 bytes kept, under a limit of 400.
    That step was given no patch at all for these files, though they appear in the summary above:
    demo/only9.md

    FILES IN THIS RANGE
    demo/only7.md | 4 ++++
    demo/only8.md | 4 ++++
    demo/only9.md | 4 ++++
    3 files changed, 12 insertions(+)
    diff --git a/demo/only7.md b/demo/only7.md
    …

**That is Q-0128's disclosure reaching a human at the gate** rather than a reviewer's prompt, which
is the thing four earlier tickets were reviewed without.

### The honest no-diff case, also transcribed

At the same run's **implement** gate — a step that reads no diff — the screen says:

    The step whose decision reached this gate was given no diff, so there is nothing to show here.
    That is not a claim that nothing changed: most of the flows this product ships review no diff at
    all, and a gate declared by a flow can follow any step.

Correct there, and it names the condition rather than implying an empty change.

### A measured limitation, recorded rather than left to be found

**On `review.yaml` the gate shows no diff, and that is the implementation matching AC-2 rather than a
bug.** Its deciding step is `verdict`, whose input is the panel's reports and whose own instruction
reads *"Judge the reviews, not the code diff."* The two **panel** members read the diff and declare
no verdict. So AC-2's model — the gate serves the *deciding* step's evidence — holds on `chore`,
where one step both reads and decides, and yields *no diff* on the flow named for reviewing. Worth
its own ticket; not repaired here, because which of two panel members' diffs a gate should show is a
design question rather than a hand fix.

### Cleaned up

Run aborted, daemon stopped, scratch ticket `Q-0136`, its run history, both its branches and both
worktrees removed, and `harness/harness.yaml` restored — `max_diff_bytes` back to 200000 and the
`adapterOverride` gone.

## GO-4 — the hand pass, and GO-6

**GO-4.** All three reviews were truncated — 73.6%, 71.2%, 69.5% — on the **same** 13 files, among
them `packages/shared/src/diff-evidence.ts` and the whole of the daemon route. The omitted tail was
**87,100 bytes**, reviewed by hand cross-vendor with the governing rulings quoted. It returned two
findings: one **confirmed** — `diffEvidenceSchema` declared `truncated`, `kept` and `total` as
independent fields while the docblock four lines above said they *"cannot disagree"*, so
`{ truncated: false, kept: 10, total: 20 }` parsed — and one **refuted**, that `evidenceFor` leaks
across runs, which it does not: it keys by `(handle, gateId)` throughout and the contract defines
`gateId` as unique *within one run*. Both recorded; the first fixed and shown red by mutation.

**GO-6.** Verified forced in both environment rows — a detached worktree with neither
`.harness/worktrees` nor `.quorum/runs`, and `main` after the merge — **7/7 tasks 0 cached** in each,
`pnpm lint` and `pnpm typecheck` 7/7, `quorum lint` 6/6, and the git-identity sweep green.
